    Fix: surgical DOM updates for checkbox toggle to prevent element detachment

    The toggle checkbox handlers (single item and toggle-all) previously called
    this.render() which destroyed and recreated all <li> elements via innerHTML.
    In a real browser, Cypress chains commands on elements after clicking; when
    the elements are destroyed mid-chain, Cypress reports 'element detached from DOM'.

    Now toggle operations modify existing <li> elements in place (toggling the
    completed class and checkbox state) instead of rebuilding the DOM tree.
    Filtered views are also handled: items that no longer match the current
    filter are removed from the DOM rather than hidden.

